 supporting research, a lot of habitat work and a lot of policy. So, um, our executive director,

00:46:16.920 --> 00:46:23.470
 Scott Hoffman Black, worked a lot with the Obama administration on the, uh, presidential memorandum,

00:46:23.470 --> 00:46:31.020
 uh, to, uh, for pollinator conservation, which basically guided a lot of agencies like the USDA,

00:46:31.020 --> 00:46:37.020
 the Forest Service to come up with best management practices for pollinators. Um, and those are being

00:46:37.020 --> 00:46:42.620
 rolled out. And so a lot of organizations are now starting to think about how pollinators,

00:46:43.010 --> 00:46:47.510
 you know, think about them and their work and, and doing things to conserve them.

