 around your workplace or whatever, whatever, I know everybody has different access to outside

00:47:11.780 --> 00:47:15.220
 space, but like what, what are the right things to do and what do you look out for?

00:47:15.220 --> 00:47:21.630
 Yeah, that's a great question. So in my home, we only had a tiny parking strip between, you know,

00:47:21.630 --> 00:47:27.630
 where we park and the sidewalk. And so we took out the lawn and put in some drought tolerant native

00:47:27.630 --> 00:47:33.870
 plants and then around those sprinkled wildflower seeds. So trying to make sure to have, you know,

00:47:33.870 --> 00:47:40.590
 as local native plants, uh, native bees as their name tend to focus on native plants because that's

00:47:40.590 --> 00:47:46.830
 what they evolved with. They prefer them to ornamental plants. Often a lot of ornamental plants look really

00:47:46.830 --> 00:47:52.590
 pretty, but don't provide pollen and nectar. And so trying to avoid those, those often the really

00:47:52.590 --> 00:47:59.150
 ornamental ones are, have been treated with pesticides in some cases, neonicotinoids. And so might actually

00:47:59.150 --> 00:48:05.320
 be little ecological traps for the bees when you put them out. Um, and then if you're trying to support

00:48:05.320 --> 00:48:10.680
 nesting, a lot of people love mulching to get rid of weeds. And I think that that's a great way,

00:48:10.680 --> 00:48:16.600
